{% comment %}
  Fast path to ordering for clients who already have a profile on file.

  The Premium page has to do two jobs at once: sell a niche service to someone
  who has never heard of it, and get out of the way of a returning client who
  just wants to send in four rolls. Those pull in opposite directions — the
  explaining has to come first for one and not at all for the other.

  This strip resolves that. It sits directly under the hero, addresses the
  returning client by name, and links straight to the product pages. Everything
  below it is for the first-time reader, who can ignore this and carry on.

  It links rather than adding to cart, for the same reason the sticky order bar
  does: Globo puts required options on the service products (Negative
  Condition, Scan Size, Rush), so the product page is a mandatory stop and an
  add-to-cart here would skip fields the lab needs.

  Products come from the premium collection and are bucketed by the same format
  and process tags the rest of the processing catalog uses, so a format that is
  unlisted in the admin disappears from here on its own.

  Usage:
    {% render 'cfl-premium-quickorder' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign premium_collection = collections['premium-film-service']
  assign service_tag = 'Film Processing'
  assign format_keys = '35mm,medium format' | split: ','
  assign format_labels = '35mm,Medium Format' | split: ','
  assign process_keys = 'c41,bw' | split: ','
  assign process_labels = 'C-41,B&W' | split: ','
-%}

{%- if premium_collection != blank and premium_collection.products.size > 0 -%}
  <aside class="cfl-quickorder" aria-labelledby="cfl-quickorder-title">
    <div class="cfl-quickorder__intro">
      <p class="cfl-quickorder__title" id="cfl-quickorder-title">Already a Premium client?</p>
      <p class="cfl-quickorder__sub">
        Your profile is on file — order straight away.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="cfl-quickorder__list" role="list">
      {%- for format_key in format_keys -%}
        {%- assign format_label = format_labels[forloop.index0] -%}
        {%- for process_key in process_keys -%}
          {%- assign process_label = process_labels[forloop.index0] -%}

          {%- for product in premium_collection.products -%}
            {%- if product.tags contains service_tag
                and product.tags contains format_key
                and product.tags contains process_key
            -%}
              <li>
                <a class="cfl-quickorder__pill" href="{{ product.url }}">
                  <span class="cfl-quickorder__fmt">{{ format_label }}</span>
                  <span class="cfl-quickorder__proc">{{ process_label }}</span>
                  <span class="cfl-quickorder__price">{{ product.price | money }}</span>
                </a>
              </li>
              {%- break -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}

        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </aside>
{%- endif -%}
